# oxfmt ignore patterns (oxfmt reads .prettierignore by default; prettier itself
# is not used here).
#
# Everything in this repository is formatted, including metadata retrieved from
# the org. The repository is the source of truth for its org — we deploy from
# force-app — so our formatting standard applies to what it contains.
#
# The exception is build output. Minified files are not source: formatting one
# produces a meaningless diff, destroys the identity of the distributed
# artifact, and turns every dependency upgrade into a huge unreviewable change.
# This is the same reason every JavaScript project keeps dist/ and node_modules/
# out of its formatter.
#
# In a Salesforce repository these arrive as static resources — a vendored
# jquery.min.js and the like.
**/*.min.js
**/*.min.css

# Vendored assets that are not minified belong here too. Nothing in the metadata
# marks a static resource as third-party, so it has to be declared by whoever
# adds it. This file is deliberately NOT in .templatesyncignore, so entries you
# add here survive template sync.
#   Directory-type resource: force-app/main/default/staticresources/<name>/**
#   Single-file resource:    force-app/main/default/staticresources/<name>.js
